        answer: "Both, and often together. Storm surge pushes up the Patapsco from the Chesapeake Bay and over the bulkheads, while intense rainfall floods streets and overwhelms drains - worse when the harbor is already high and outfalls are submerged. Effective mitigation designs for the compound event, not one source in isolation.",
